TEXT -456 -96 Left 5 ;That means if parallel line is shut down\nCE is 7.65nF more than 5.57nF per system like for the double system \nThis is important for the petersen !!!!!!!
TEXT -248 152 Left 2 ;See file:\nMeasurement_of_CE_1150kV_6x680_85_only_one_system.wxmx\nfor the measurment of CEequivalent and Ipet and Lpet
TEXT 32 16 Left 2 ;NOTE: The nominal current of the petersen is more than\nhalve the value of the two system configuration\nsince the second line (isolated) are capacitive coupled\nto the first line (and therefore under voltage)\nand delivering additional current to earth\n(and to the petersen)
TEXT -544 64 Left 2 ;NOTE:\nFor transient simulation\nyou have to change the\nvoltage source model to\nv_3phase !!
TEXT 32 96 Left 2 ;The cap. Value to earth of the phases are as follows:\nPhase1: 5.1nF (see as waveform: I(u2:C_10a)/V(n002)/314.159\nPhase2: 4.28nF (see as waveform: I(u2:C_20a)/V(n005)/314.159\nPhase3: 7.3nF (see as waveform: I(u2:C_30a)/V(n008)/314.159\nAverage: 5.56nF
TEXT -496 176 Left 2 ;NOTE: You can see that at the resonant\npoint the starpoint voltage is far\nto high (even higher as the nominal system \nvoltage)\nThis is due to the big differences of the\nreactances of the different phases!\nTherefore the phases needs to be crossed out (transposed)\nSee file Petersen_2sys_crossedout.asc
TEXT 32 152 Left 2 ;The cap. Values of the second line are the same\nbut they are operating under a smaller voltage\nand also contributing to the total earth current\nThe resulting equivalent cap. value is 7.65nF\n(5.57nF for line1 and additionaly 2.08nF for line2\n68% of double line circuit
TEXT -376 112 Left 2 ;CE_equivalent: 7.64nF
TEXT -376 56 Left 2 ;NOTE:\nTo tune the petersen nominal current:\nAt the compensation point the resonant curve\nof the petersen (starpoint) voltage has\na maximum value at nominal frequncy (50Hz)
